    <briefdescription>
<para>A list of <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_d_i_e" kindref="compound">DIE</ref> values. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This is a singly-linked list, but instead of reversing the order of insertion, we keep a pointer to the back of the list so we can push in order.</para>
<para>There are two main reasons to choose a linked list over a customized vector-like data structure.</para>
<para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>For teardown efficiency, we want DIEs to be BumpPtrAllocated. Using a linked list here makes this way easier to accomplish.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Carrying an extra pointer per <emphasis><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_d_i_e_value" kindref="compound">DIEValue</ref></emphasis> isn&apos;t expensive. 45% of DIEs have 2 or fewer values, and 90% have 5 or fewer. A vector would be over-allocated by 50% on average anyway, the same cost as the linked-list node. </para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
